# Owner directives (highest priority; supersede roadmap/CI/portability wording)

1. **macOS only initially.** Apple Silicon, macOS 13+. No Linux or Windows code, CI jobs, runners, shims, packaging or portability work until the owner lifts this.
2. Keep platform code isolated behind `platform/` interfaces (clean seams only; no stubs or ports for other OSes).
3. CI/dev scripts target macOS only. Skip any roadmap item for Linux/Windows (M11, M12) and cross-platform CI matrices.
# C17 coding standard

This document is normative. Changes to ABI, ownership, threading, or source
preservation require an ADR.

## Names and structure

- Use C17, four-space indentation, LF, and `snake_case` identifiers.
- Prefix exported symbols with their module (`svg_`, `ui_`, `raster_`).
- Keep public contracts in headers and module ownership/tests in a short README.
- Prefer small functions with early error returns. Comments explain invariants,
  units, lifetime, and non-obvious choices.
- Keep source files below 800 lines; split modules before they grow further.

## Ownership and memory

- State whether each pointer is owned or borrowed and how long it stays valid.
- Use pointer+length slices; never infer length from a missing terminator.
- Use arenas or module allocators. Avoid allocation in hot loops.
- Check addition, multiplication, and capacity growth before allocation.
- Do not use VLAs, `alloca`, `strcpy`, `strcat`, `sprintf`, or unchecked format
  construction. No implicit null-termination assumptions.
- Do not retain pointers into growable buffers or pass unowned pointers between
  threads. OOM must not leave a partial edit committed.

## Errors, parsing, and assertions

- Malformed input, resource limits, unsupported features, and OOM are normal
  errors, not assertions.
- Assertions document impossible internal invariants only.
- Bound bytes, nodes, nesting, expansion, pixels, and work queues.
- Never load network resources or execute SVG scripts. Preserve unknown source
  spans and namespaces.
- Define behavior for overflow, NaN/Inf, invalid matrices, malformed UTF-8,
  invalid path flags, and zero divisors.
- Avoid recursion over user-controlled depth unless an explicit depth budget is
  checked.

## Concurrency and rendering

- Mutate documents on the UI thread. Workers read immutable snapshots and
  publish owned results tagged with a generation.
- Cancel, drain, and join workers before releasing snapshots or source buffers.
- Scalar rendering is deterministic and is the reference for optimized paths.
- Keep allocation out of pixel loops and record performance counters at module
  boundaries.

## Verification

Use only build, test, sanitizer, fuzz, format, lint, and benchmark commands
implemented by the active work order. Run required checks explicitly and record
their results. Benchmarks must include machine, compiler, build type, workload,
and raw measurements. Never claim a speedup without a reproducible baseline.
# ADR 0002: Source preservation and provenance

- Status: accepted
- Date: 2026-10-08
- Decision owner: project owner

## Context

SVG documents contain formatting, metadata, namespaces, and unsupported content
that may not be represented by the first rendering subset. A destructive parse
and reserialization would lose information before editing fidelity is known.

## Decisions

- Retain original input bytes and source spans. A no-op save must be byte exact.
- Preserve unknown XML/SVG subtrees and namespaces when editing supported data.
- Treat scripts, external entities, and external resource loads as unsupported
  and do not execute or fetch them.
- External algorithms and all vendored code/assets need source URL, exact
  revision, cryptographic hash, license, rationale, and an adapter boundary in
  `docs/provenance.md` and `third_party/README.md` before inclusion.
- Do not inspect, fetch, or copy GPL SVG-editor implementation source. Standards
  documents and file-format descriptions are allowed.

## Consequences

Parser and editing APIs carry source ranges and explicit limits. Unsupported
features must be surfaced rather than silently dropped. Vendor or corpus
changes require a dedicated work order and license review.

## Sources

- `docs/research-r3/plan/04-coding-standard.md` (source spans and safety limits).
- `docs/research-r4/06-risks-and-safety.md` (untrusted document inputs).
# Bounded XML tokenizer

`svg_xml_tokenize` reads a borrowed `base_bytes` view and writes caller-owned
`svg_xml_token` entries. It never allocates, reads files, resolves entities,
normalizes line endings, or mutates input. Every span is a half-open byte range
into the exact original UTF-8 input; attribute value and comment/PI/text/CDATA
content spans exclude their delimiters. QName `prefix` is empty when absent;
`local_name` is always populated. Namespaces are not resolved. Token data is
valid only while the caller's input remains alive and unchanged.

The scanner is iterative, linear in input length plus the bounded attribute
and name comparisons, and uses a fixed 256-entry element-name stack. Duplicate
attribute detection compares prior attribute tokens for the current element,
so the worst case is quadratic in attributes on that element. No recursion or
heap allocation occurs. On any failure `token_count` and success counts are
zero and `diagnostic` contains a stable category and an offset in `[0,input.len]`.
Output exhaustion is an ordinary diagnostic.

Defaults are 16 MiB input, 256 nested elements, 1,000,000 nodes,
4,096 attributes per element, 1,000,000 attributes total, and 4 MiB per
character-data or CDATA run. Names are additionally capped at 4,096 UTF-8
bytes as a fixed implementation bound. The caller can lower each configurable
cap but cannot raise it; depth cannot exceed the fixed 256-entry stack. A node is an
element, comment, PI, in-element text run, or CDATA run. XML declaration is
not a node. Whitespace outside the document element is tokenized but does not
count as a node.

Accepted syntax includes XML 1.0 documents encoded as UTF-8 with an optional
leading BOM, XML declaration,
PI, comments, element and empty-element tags, quoted attributes, character
data, and CDATA. Predefined and numeric references are retained lexically;
custom entity references are rejected because DTDs are unsupported. Every
DOCTYPE/ENTITY declaration is rejected at its opening byte. No namespace URI
resolution, DTD, external entity, serializer, or tree is provided. XML 1.0
character and Name character ranges are validated; encoding declarations must
say UTF-8. Line endings and entity spellings are never normalized.
#ifndef VEXEL_XML_TOKENIZER_H
#define VEXEL_XML_TOKENIZER_H

#include "base.h"

#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdint.h>

typedef enum svg_xml_token_kind {
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_DECLARATION = 1,
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_PROCESSING_INSTRUCTION,
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_COMMENT,
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_START_ELEMENT,
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_END_ELEMENT,
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_EMPTY_ELEMENT,
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_ATTRIBUTE,
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_TEXT,
    SVG_XML_TOKEN_CDATA
} svg_xml_token_kind;

typedef enum svg_xml_error {
    SVG_XML_ERROR_NONE = 0,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_INPUT_LIMIT,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_INVALID_UTF8,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_INVALID_CHARACTER,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_ENCODING,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_INVALID_NAME,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_MALFORMED_SYNTAX,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_DUPLICATE_ATTRIBUTE,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_MISMATCHED_TAG,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_DEPTH_LIMIT,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_NODE_LIMIT,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_ATTRIBUTE_LIMIT,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_TEXT_LIMIT,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_OUTPUT_EXHAUSTED,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_DTD,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_MULTIPLE_ROOTS,
    SVG_XML_ERROR_INCOMPLETE_DOCUMENT
} svg_xml_error;

typedef struct svg_xml_span {
    size_t offset;
    size_t length;
} svg_xml_span;

typedef struct svg_xml_token {
    svg_xml_token_kind kind;
    svg_xml_span source;
    svg_xml_span name;
    svg_xml_span value;
    svg_xml_span prefix;
    svg_xml_span local_name;
    size_t depth;
} svg_xml_token;

typedef struct svg_xml_limits {
    size_t input_bytes;
    size_t nesting_depth;
    size_t nodes;
    size_t attributes_per_element;
    size_t total_attributes;
    size_t text_run_bytes;
} svg_xml_limits;

typedef struct svg_xml_options {
    svg_xml_limits limits;
} svg_xml_options;

typedef struct svg_xml_diagnostic {
    svg_xml_error category;
    size_t offset;
} svg_xml_diagnostic;

typedef struct svg_xml_result {
    size_t token_count;
    size_t element_count;
    size_t attribute_count;
    size_t node_count;
    svg_xml_diagnostic diagnostic;
} svg_xml_result;

svg_xml_options svg_xml_default_options(void);
svg_xml_result svg_xml_tokenize(base_bytes input, svg_xml_options options,
                                svg_xml_token *tokens, size_t token_capacity);
const char *svg_xml_error_name(svg_xml_error error);

#endif
